.TH QUANUXCTL-INFRA 1 "March 2026" "QuanuX" "QuanuX Control Manual"
.SH NAME
quanuxctl-infra \- QuanuX Control Plane: Ephemeral Infrastructure Provisioning
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quanuxctl infra
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B quanuxctl infra
manages the physical hardware and logical network boundaries for the QuanuX ecosystem. It directly interfaces with Terraform to deploy 0-Trust environments across cloud providers like DigitalOcean and Google Cloud Platform. 

.SH COMMANDS
.B Storage Authentication:
.TP
.B set-token \fItoken\fR
Securely saves the DigitalOcean API Token to the native OS Keyring. Zero-disk footprint.
.TP
.B set-spaces-keys \fIaccess\fR \fIsecret\fR
Securely saves DO Spaces keys to the OS Keyring.

.B Provisioning Pipeline:
.TP
.B auth
Retrieves provider credentials from OS Keyring (DO) or local identity files (GCP) and outputs bash export strings for Terraform parsing.
Usage: \fBeval $(quanuxctl infra auth --target [do|gcp])\fR
.TP
.B apply
Executes `terraform apply` targeting the designated provider zero-trust VPC and matrix structure.
Usage: \fBquanuxctl infra apply --target [do|gcp]\fR
.TP
.B destroy
Tears down the designated provider zero-trust environment using `terraform destroy`.
Usage: \fBquanuxctl infra destroy --target [do|gcp]\fR
.TP
.B status
Lists active node public and internal IPs by resolving the designated provider's terraform state. Also lists the active Sovereign Vault bucket.
Usage: \fBquanuxctl infra status --target [do|gcp]\fR

.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on complete provisioning execution or correct state parsing.
Returns 1 on Terraform errors, missing keys, or unreachable environments.
